"""Measured M7 reports; results are research, never automatic promotion evidence."""
from pathlib import Path
import json
import pandas as pd
from .reporting import table


def comparison_report(run):
    run=Path(run);c=pd.read_csv(run/'comparison.csv');selection=json.loads((run/'selection.json').read_text())
    subset=c[c.period.eq('examined_2024_2025')&c.reference.eq('boosting')]
    lines=['# M7 exploratory ensemble comparison','',f"Development-selected ensemble: `{selection['method']}`. Development-selected strongest individual: `{selection['strongest_individual']}`. Policy selection uses 2022–2023 only; annual fitted parameters use earlier OOS labels under the frozen calendar.",'',table(subset[['model','metric','estimate','difference','difference_low','difference_high','games']]),'', 'Deltas are model minus annual-refit M5-architecture boosting. Lower Brier/log loss and higher accuracy are better. See comparison.csv for logistic and strongest-individual references, each year, and development scores. These are matched M7 annual predictions, not a reproduction of M5’s frozen-2022 artifact.','', 'Intervals are paired season-week bootstrap percentiles, unadjusted for examining up to 24 ensemble policies. Correlated weeks, repeated teams, few seasons and reuse of 2024–2025 preclude independent confirmation. Development selection results are not independent tests. No champion activation.']
    (run/'MODEL_COMPARISON.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')


def engineering_report(run,root):
    run=Path(run);root=Path(root);meta=json.loads((run/'metadata.json').read_text());selection=json.loads((run/'selection.json').read_text())
    c=pd.read_csv(run/'comparison.csv');exam=c[c.period.eq('examined_2024_2025')&c.reference.eq('boosting')]
    summary=exam.pivot(index='model',columns='metric',values='estimate').reset_index()
    selected=exam[exam.model.eq(selection['method'])]
    verification=root/'docs/m7/VERIFICATION.json';qa=json.loads(verification.read_text()) if verification.exists() else {'status':'Verification pending; generating this report does not establish passing tests.'}
    protocol=root/'docs/m7/PROTOCOL.md'
    per_season=c[c.reference.eq('boosting')&c.period.isin(['2024','2025'])&c.model.isin(['logistic','boosting','elo_margin',selection['method']])]
    parameters=pd.read_csv(run/'parameters.csv');parameters=parameters[parameters.model.eq(selection['method'])]
    brier=selected[selected.metric.eq('brier')].iloc[0]
    reference_brier=float(exam[exam.model.eq('boosting')&exam.metric.eq('brier')].estimate.iloc[0])
    finding=(f"The development-selected {selection['method']} scored Brier {brier.estimate:.6f} versus annual boosting {reference_brier:.6f}; "
             f"its model-minus-boosting difference was {brier.difference:+.6f}, with exploratory interval [{brier.difference_low:+.6f}, {brier.difference_high:+.6f}]. "
             "Lower is better. These examined results do not justify replacing the frozen policy with a later-period winner or promoting an ensemble.")
    correlations=pd.read_csv(run/'complementarity.csv')
    lines=['# M7 engineering report','', '## Implementation and baseline preservation','', 'M7 combines existing M2 logistic, fixed M5 shallow boosting and fixed M3 margin Elo. It adds annual OOS base caches, eight predefined raw ensemble policies, optional disjoint sigmoid/isotonic calibration, development-only selection, checksum-bound registry references, immutable experimental forecasts/results, CLI commands and Ensemble Analysis. M6 opponent/personnel code is preserved and excluded from these inputs. Production remains M2. No M8 work was performed.','', 'Before implementation the complete suite actually passed 106 tests, matching M6. Full pre-M7 source/dataset/artifact hashes and champion metadata are in docs/m7/BASELINE.json. Earlier comparison implementations are covered by the full regression suite; their old report pointers are deliberately preserved rather than rerunning them into new output generations.','', '## Chronological contract recorded before coding','',protocol.read_text() if protocol.exists() else 'See docs/m7/PROTOCOL.md.','', '## Exact fitted fold boundaries','',table(pd.DataFrame([{k:v for k,v in f.items() if k not in ['optimizer','skipped_calibrations']} for f in meta['folds']])),'', 'Annual base cutoffs, versions, training counts and source fingerprints are retained with the base matrix metadata and every row. Ensemble registry references verify exact base artifact checksums, feature schemas and training cutoffs. Margin Elo retains its original 2018 replay origin, whereas M5’s standard Elo feature retains 1999 warmup. The current production artifact is never used in historical folds.','', 'The primary comparison uses annual prior-season refits, including 2023 training for 2024 and 2024 training for 2025. This differs from the M5/M6 frozen-2022 HGB evaluation; differences from that older reported number cannot be attributed solely to ensembling. All M7 direct comparisons share the annual base matrix and identical eligible games.','', '## Alignment and exclusions','', '```json',json.dumps(meta['alignment'],indent=2),'```','', 'Ties update underlying histories but do not enter binary fitting or scoring. Incomplete and unavailable final outcomes are excluded. Missing base predictions are counted and never replaced with 0.5. These categories may overlap. No dropped row can silently create different model evaluation samples.','', '## Development selection and parameter fitting','',table(pd.read_csv(run/'development_selection.csv')),'', 'Selected policy metadata: `'+json.dumps(selection)+'`. There are eight raw policies and up to 24 ensemble/calibration configurations, plus three individual references. Equal-season development mean Brier, then log loss, then name chooses the policy. Later evaluation labels do not choose weights, representation, regularization or calibration method. Parameters are refitted annually using only the scheduled earlier meta/calibration periods.','',table(parameters),'', 'Constrained optimization uses SLSQP with an analytic gradient, nonnegative unit-sum weights and fixed .02 shrinkage toward (.2,.6,.2). The two stackers use three inputs plus intercept, L2 C=1, no interactions and deterministic seed. Exact optimizer status/weights and meta/calibration fingerprints are stored per fold. There is no base hyperparameter/window search.','', '## Measured already-examined 2024–2025 results','',finding,'',table(summary),'', 'Selected ensemble versus matched annual boosting:','',table(selected[['model','metric','estimate','difference','difference_low','difference_high','games']]),'', '## Individual seasons','',table(per_season[['period','model','metric','estimate','difference','difference_low','difference_high','games']]),'', 'comparison.csv additionally supplies matched intervals against logistic and the development-selected strongest individual. Nominal intervals are unadjusted exploratory diagnostics, not a superiority or promotion certificate.','', '## Complementarity, calibration and uncertainty','',table(correlations),'', 'Probability correlation and residual (p−y) correlation are descriptive; shared outcomes induce residual correlation. Disagreement and agreement subsets, average confidence gaps and pairwise disagreement outcomes are in pair_disagreements.csv and disagreement.csv. Elo already enters HGB as a standard-Elo feature, so algorithm names alone do not establish diversity. M7 tests margin Elo separately; no claim of causal independent contribution follows from correlation.','', 'Raw, sigmoid and supported isotonic variants are all exported. Calibrators fit only the intervening year’s OOS base probabilities transformed by the frozen meta-model. Annual deployment base models are refitted after those OOS calibration predictions were made; calibration transfer across base refits remains a limitation. Reliability diagrams, calibration slopes/intercepts, confidence buckets, early/late seasons, and model-defined favorites/underdogs are saved. Favorites use >=50% model probability, not market odds. A tie at 50% deterministically picks home.','', '## Prospective forecasts, registry and dashboard','', 'forecast-ensemble uses versioned 2026 annual base refits and the development-selected policy; it never fits models. Both source features and online Elo updates obey the chosen cutoff. Actual creation time must precede kickoff and cannot be backdated. All base/meta/calibration/selection training must precede that cutoff. Historical research rows are labeled retrospective and carry actual generation time.','', 'Experimental forecasts live under data/m7/experimental_forecasts, separately from SQLite. A game/version/cutoff identifies an immutable forecast; repeated identical issuance reuses it, while changed probabilities or provenance are rejected rather than overwriting it. Revised cutoffs/versions create separate forecasts. Result grading appends events, including revisions and ties, without modifying forecasts. Multiple forecasts for one game are correlated revisions and must not be treated as independent evidence.','', 'Registry loading verifies the ensemble checksum plus every base checksum/schema/version/cutoff; missing or incompatible artifacts are errors. Existing registry rollback and activation paths remain compatible; M7 artifacts are explicitly activation-blocked. The official champion and SQLite bytes remain preserved. Team Comparison shows only available, checksum-verified experimental saved forecasts alongside the existing champion estimate, with their own cutoffs labeled. Ensemble Analysis reads saved results and forecast records; rendering never trains or issues forecasts.','', '## Runtime and cache evidence','',table(pd.read_csv(run/'runtime.csv')),'',f"Measured research runtime: {meta['runtime_seconds']:.3f} seconds; peak RSS where measurable: {meta['peak_rss_bytes']} bytes. CPU-only, existing dependencies. Base predictions are built once per source/code/config fingerprint; weight/calibration experiments operate on compact matrices.",'', '## Verification and Windows status','', '```json',json.dumps(qa,indent=2),'```','', 'M6 was accepted as an engineering milestone by the user. Native M6 and M7 Windows execution was not independently demonstrated here. Linux tests, imports, UI checks and the provided combined Windows script do not establish native Windows acceptance.','', '## Launch and reproduce','', 'Use Python 3.12 and the locked dependencies: `python -m pip install -r requirements.lock.txt`; `python -m pip install -e ".[test]"`. Restore existing data/model caches or run documented M1/M5 ingestion first. Then run:','', '```powershell','python -m nfl_predictor.cli build-ensemble-predictions','python -m nfl_predictor.cli compare-m7','python -m nfl_predictor.cli report-m7','python -m nfl_predictor.cli forecast-ensemble','python -m nfl_predictor.cli grade-ensemble','python -m pytest -q','python -m streamlit run app.py','```','', 'Open http://localhost:8501. On genuine Windows use `.\\scripts\\windows_acceptance.ps1 -Full` for combined M6/M7 processing, then perform manual UI and memory checks. Cached results can be inspected offline. Downloaded datasets, SQLite and fitted joblib artifacts are not committed; reproducible measured reports are included.','', '## Limitations and promotion recommendation','', 'Retain M2 as the official champion. Any future promotion needs explicit approval, independent prospective evidence and native Windows verification. Development chooses among up to 24 correlated policies; repeatedly examined 2024–2025 is exploratory. Schedule/model/data vintages and final-publication timestamps remain retrospective. The inherited eight-hour eligibility proxy and date-only historical bounds remain assumptions. Personnel coverage is still insufficient and deliberately unused. No probability is called calibrated merely because a calibration transform was applied.','', 'For M8 planning only: first collect independent prospective outcomes and verify Windows behavior. Any proposed Betting Lab must be separately scoped and approved; no odds, wagering, expected-value calculations or M8 implementation were added.']
    path=root/'M7_ENGINEERING_REPORT.md';path.write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf-8');return path
